    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d110">

                <pb facs="0400" n="352" sameAs="frus:frus1868p1/pg352"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Johnson</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 18.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-09-17"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 17, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I inclose a copy of an instruction of the
                    8th instant to Mr. J. Ross Browne, United States minister at Peking, relative to
                    a contemplated revision of the tariff and revenue parts of our former treaty
                    with China.</p>
                <p>This paper is furnished you, as is indicated therein, with a view to its being
                    used, if necessary, in preserving and maintaining a good understanding with the
                    British government in regard to the important subjects to which it relates.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Reverdy Johnson,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
